Tranche 2 Deliverable 2: the three feeds, and where each number comes from.

The reviewer: "USDC_USD and EF_BOND are not sourced from Reflector or Etherfuse
and nothing on chain reads them: please wire the sources and say what the peg
feed is meant to gate."

== USDC_USD, from Reflector

  oracle        CCYOZJCOPG34LLQQ7N24YXBM7LL62R7ONMZ3G6WZAAYPB5OYKOMJRN63 (testnet, SEP-40)
  call          lastprice(Other("USDC"))
  base          USD, 14 decimals, 300s resolution
  read          100130125419644 at 1793374500
  rescaled      10013012 at 7 decimals, which is 1.0013012
  freshness     153s old against a limit of two resolution periods
  submitted     quorum of 2, NavQuorumReached, NavUpdated
  our feed      10000001 -> 10013012

  Read on chain by Vault::require_peg on every deposit. Gates deposit, refusing
  outside 200 bps of par with PegBroken (331). Demonstrated by
  scripts/e2e-peg-gate.sh, 11 assertions.

== EF_BOND, from Etherfuse

  endpoint      https://api.etherfuse.com/lookup/bonds/cost/USTRY  (public, no auth)
  bond          USTRY, the US Treasury stablebond, in USD
                CETES is the same instrument in pesos and would put an FX leg
                inside a USD NAV, so it is not the one.
  read          1.078704 USD per unit, yield 369 bps
  sources       5 of 5 inside 900s, ages 13 to 63s, 0.0 bps from their median
  rescaled      10787040 at 7 decimals
  submitted     quorum of 2, NavQuorumReached, NavUpdated
  our feed      10362600 -> 10787040, a 409 bps move

  Read on chain by EtherfuseAdapter::oracle_value and price_drift_bps.

  Why the cross-source check is in the keeper and not in the Adapter: EF_BOND is
  registered with a zero deviation bound, because the award calls that NAV
  deterministic. The Adapter will therefore accept any move inside its band, so
  the quality of the number is entirely the quality of its sourcing. A single
  drifted source is exactly what a zero deviation bound cannot catch.

== PC_NAV, from a servicing tape

  source        data/servicing/tape-2026-10-30.csv, sha256 in the run log
  computed      scripts/reconcile-nav.py, a pure function of the tape and the date
  read          10374235, which is 1.0374235
  submitted     quorum of 2 at timestamp 1793372104
  distributed   1897996 stroops, exchange_rate 17138171 -> 17143622

  Not refreshed by a cron. A tape arrives on the originator's cadence and the
  staleness window is seven days to match, so keeper-oracle.sh reports how much
  of the window is left and says so loudly when it is running out. Reposting the
  stored value was the dishonest way to keep it fresh and is gone.

== What each keeper refuses to do

  keeper-reflector.sh    will not submit when Reflector itself is more than two
                         of its own resolution periods behind. Pushing a stale
                         number under a current timestamp forges a freshness it
                         did not get, and the Adapter cannot detect that: it
                         judges the timestamp it is handed.

  keeper-etherfuse.sh    will not submit when fewer than three sources are
                         recent, when they disagree by more than 50 bps around
                         their median, or when the bond is not denominated in USD.

  both                   check our own feed's minimum interval first. Without
                         that the first reporter's vote lands and stays pending,
                         so a keeper that ran too soon left a half-finished
                         round behind every time.
